    {
      "field_name": "diagnostic_criteria",
      "value": "clinical features (stiffness, spasms, sensory-enhanced tone, opsoclonus, encephalopathy), antibody detection (anti-amphiphysin in serum and CSF), treatment response to plasmapheresis",
      "quote": "Muscle tone in the right arm and trunk erectors was markedly increased and further enhanced by sensory stimuli. CSF showed 6 cells/ /H9262L, increased protein (117 mg/dL), and identical oligoclonal bands to serum. Anti-GAD, anti Yo, and anti-Hu antibodies were negative, but high titer antiamphiphysin antibodies were detected in the patient’s serum and CSF (Dr. Seelig, Karlsruhe, Germany). Plasma exchange treatment (PE) was initiated 10 weeks after the first symptoms had started. During a series of 11 PE, the increased muscle tone was normalized, and the patient was able to walk again with help, associated with a 16-fold drop of the serum anti-amphiphysin antibody titers (1: 3, 280, 000 to 1: 205, 000; figure 1a).",
      "confidence": "high"
    },
